Working on a "eating wands" patch.

The patch creates the following effects when certain wands are eaten:
	slow monster/speed monster - same as zapping
	enlightenment/make invisible/polymorph - same as potion
	light - levitation (_light_er)
	magic missile/striking - 1 to 5 * charges damage, if you die,
		the message is "unusual diet"
	cold/fire - if not cold/fire resistant, 1 to 7 * charges
		damage, if you die, message is also "unusual diet".
		Chance of opposite resistance.
	lightning - if not resistant, 1 to 7 * charges damage, 
		chance of resistance, same death message.
	locking - if non-negative luck, chance of disintigration
		resistance (locks you together), else, chance of
		stoning (credit to Swervy_a).
	sleep - chance of sleep resistance if you don't have it, if that 
		fails, you fall asleep.
	cancellation - random intrinsic removed (same as gremlin attack)
	death - instantly fatal (death message: "foolishly ate a wand of
		death")
	digging - if you are not near hungry, it makes you more hungry.
		If you are near hungry, it does 1 + 5 * charges damage.
	teleportation - makes you teleport, chance of teleportitis,
		small chance of teleport control if blessed.

I consider this rather balanced -- by the time you can polymorph into a
monster that can eat wands, you should have the chance for most of
these intrinsics.

However, the following wands have no effects yet:

	undead turning ( I was considering that this should make the
		player into an undead V, M, Z, L, or W, but the code 
		for that would be complex, and most players would have 
		polymorph control by the time they are eating this wand.
		Ideas? )
	secret door detection
	create monster ( should this make you satiated? )
	nothing ( perhaps this should have no effect? )
	opening ( should this make you hungry, like /oDigging? )
	probin
	wishing
	
I'm also thinking that most wands should have a chance to gain energy,
similar to a !oEnergy -- perhaps, say, from 1 to 2 * charges (4 *
charges if blessed).

I'm happy with most of this, but would like a few wildcard effects
thrown in, since the player will be eating charged magical objects.  Any
ideas?

